      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess this works for now, but the structure feels wrong. \nAt the very least the thing that maps requests to responses should be somewhere outside this function, probably outside this file.\nAnd the lifetime of the stream feels a bit weird.\n\nDo we need a DataChannel class at all? The calling code is:\n    let mut data_channel \u003d DataChannel::from(socket_device);\n    data_channel.connect(host_addr())?;\n    data_channel.handle_incoming_request()?;\n    data_channel.force_close()?;\n    \nShould it be more like\nlet mut stream \u003d VsockStream::from(socket_device, host_addr())?;\n\u003cloop reading requests \u0026 sending responses\u003e\n\u003cdrop stream, closing things down\u003e",
